[38;5;246m[48;5;237m❯ [38;5;231mWrite a 300-word poem about a river. Do not use any tools.[39m

[38;5;231m[49m⏺[39m Вірш англійською, як ви й просили.

  [1mThe River Keeps Its Own Counsel[0m

  Before the town had roads or names,
  the river already knew the way.
  It carved the stone one patient grain at a time,
  and never once asked the mountain for permission.

  Morning finds it silver, loose with light.
  Children dip their feet and shriek at the cold.
  An old fisherman mends his net on the bank,
  his hands moving the way the current moves,
  without hurry, without doubt.

  Downstream, the water turns to glass
